# Copy this file to .env in the root of the project you run /qa-bot:qa-run from, and fill in real values.
# .env must be gitignored - never commit secrets.
#
# The file must exist (even if empty): the plugin's Playwright MCP server loads it via --secrets at startup,
# and API requests load it into a shell subshell. Claude never reads it. Secrets are referenced by *name*
# and substituted outside the model.
#
# Because a shell also loads this file, single-quote any value containing spaces, $ or quotes:
# PROJ_STAGING_QA_PASSWORD='p@ss word$1'
#
# Add only secrets here (passwords, tokens, API keys) - one var per secret that context/<PROJECT_KEY>.md
# references by name. Write URLs and other non-secret values directly in the context file instead.
# PROJ_STAGING_QA_PASSWORD=
# PROJ_STAGING_API_TOKEN=
